\taxon{Remark}
\title{Connection normalization and fermion coefficients}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{\ref{fdip-00IV} gives #{\langle1\rangle_U=1}, #{\langle1\rangle=1}, #{\mathcal Z(0,0)=1} and
##{\langle F\rangle=\int\langle F\rangle_U\,\extd\nu(U).}
The factor changing the connection weight is #{\det K_U}. In [real positive Gaussian elimination](fdip-000D), a different coefficient and reference measure give an inverse square root determinant. Here #{\nu} is a positive measure on ordinary connections, while the fermion operation is a finite exterior-algebra coefficient functional.}
